  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Valepaska. Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: "Valepaska is a Finnish bluffing/shedding game variant of Paskahousu. 3-8 players. Cards played face-down with declarations — players can LIE about what they played. Other players call 'Valepaska!' to challenge. Wrong challenger picks up pile; caught liar picks up pile. Special cards: 2s (supercards), 10s clear pile, Aces clear face cards, four-of-a-kind clears.",
    objective: 'Shed all cards first. Last player = loser (paskahousu).',
    gameplay: "Play equal or higher rank face-down + declare. Can BLUFF. 'Valepaska!' challenge: bluffer picks up pile if caught, challenger picks up if wrong. Draw to 5. Special: 2=supercard, 10=clears 3-9, A=clears face cards, 4-of-a-kind=clears.",
